     <img src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/image/line1.gif">
   
			<table border="1" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="600">    
		<tbody><tr valign="top">
		
			<td width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b>Tony</b>
			
					| <a href="mailto:cc_jo@yahoo.com" style="pointer-events: none;"><font color="#000000"><img border="0" src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/cgi-bin/comment/mail.gif"></font></a>
					
		</font></td></tr>
		
   <tr valign="top"> <td bgcolor="#ffffd0" width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000">
			
		While many people in the world choose one side or the other, few people make that decision without making it a matter of religion. <br>Americans are heavily biased in this regard especially when our 'moral majority' (which is actually a minority) says we must back the 'chosen people' of Israel. <br>Why? Because Christ is coming. Gimme a break. But why do you think Israel gets 4 Billion US dollars a year in military aid?<br>But the Bush administration had better not think about committing US forces in this conflict as it's hinting at....see "Pentagon plan seeks countries' OK to attack Terrorist cells"<br>http://www.washtimes.com/national/20020805-27541618.htm<br>or he'll lose alot of the military on breach of contract.<br>The military has an oath of enlistment, which states <br>1) "I will support and defend the constitution against all enemies both foreign and domestic." and <br>2) I will obey the orders of the president..... As this reads, if the orders of the president (2) commits American forces to this conflict, a clear violation of the constitution (1), the he becomes a 'domestic' enemy. It rises a big Separation of Church and State Issue<br>I say look at the numbers.... Palestinians have killed 600 Israelis. The Israelis have killed nearly 1600 Palestinians. It doesn't look like they need our help that much, does it.<br>Terrorists? Look at the numbers.... 72.... seventy-two. In the current uprising (since Sept. 2000) seventy-two Palestinians were killed BEFORE the first suicide bombings. Who's the terrorist? Since then it's been tit for tat. But across the board, it's been the same proportions. Both sides are killing the innocent. Both sides are killing women and children.<br>
		<div align="right">
		<i>9 August 2002</i>
		
			<i> - USA</i>
			
		</div>
		
		</font></td></tr>
		
		</tbody></table>
		
     <img src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/image/line1.gif">
   
			<table border="1" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="600">    
		<tbody><tr valign="top">
		
			<td width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b>melanie carrel</b>
			
					| <a href="mailto:danmel69@juno.com" style="pointer-events: none;"><font color="#000000"><img border="0" src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/cgi-bin/comment/mail.gif"></font></a>
					
		</font></td></tr>
		
    <tr valign="top"> <td bgcolor="#fffff0" width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000">
			
		As the mother of a daughter (Samarra) who is half Palestinian it saddens me that she has to hear all the negative press about one part of her geneology and never hear all the positives except from her father and I. As a human being it saddens me that in a supposedly forward thinking country we allow a people in a different country to be oppressed and violated on a daily person by colonists who beleive they are able to take land because they belong to a religion. The U.S. labels Palestinians terrorists yet we do not not dare label American Indian's forefathers terrorists and yes they killed civillian settlers women children etc.. They too fought against settlers on their land. Our leaders don't see the hypocrisy in supporting a people that take lands and moving the people that have lived there for generations into "refugee" camps just because somewhere in their religious history they might have once lived there and yet the native peoples of the U.S. aren't given their choice of their (historically proven) country back. We are not moving non Native American descendents to refugee camps on land the Native Americans delegate to us. Yet going by the reasons we support israel we should. I would also like to remind pro-Israelis that Adolf Hitler never called them concentration camps he called the "REFUGEE CAMPS". Maybe the jewish people learned some bad ideas from the Nazis because refugee camps and confiscating land<br> homes etc. sounds like gestapo tactics to me. Remember the ghettos, curfews etc.? I would also like to know where all the Jews were when Muslims in the former Soviet Union were going through a holocost of their own with the lovely title of ethnic cleansing. It is tragic that there was a Jewish holucost but you don't get to have your own country built on the lives of others because of it. If the jews wanted another country they should have bought some desert and built one from the ground up. What would happen if EVERY religion and sect thereof wanted their own country? WWWIII
		<div align="right">
		<i>6 August 2002</i>
		
			<i> - u.s.a.</i>
			
		</div>
		
		</font></td></tr>
		
		</tbody></table>
		
     <img src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/image/line1.gif">
   
			<table border="1" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="600">    
		<tbody><tr valign="top">
		
			<td width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b>Michael Ross</b>
			
		</font></td></tr>
		
   <tr valign="top"> <td bgcolor="#ffffd0" width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000">
			
		Dear "Upset Jew" - didn't you know that Jewish Zionist terrorists in the 1940's bombed the King David Hotel, killing around 100 people? Terrorists always kill innocents.<br>Hundreds of thousands of Palestinians were displaced from their homes and livlihoods, at gunpoint and by force, and many were killed who resisted, because the Zionists believed that the land should belong to them.<br>They were wrong, and it was immoral. <br>Israel exists now, and the Arab nations have agreed to recognize it, which is good. All the peoples must learn to live together and treat each other fairly.<br>But Israel must admit its past injustice and try to make up for it. This is the only way forward... as long as they deny their own past brutality they will continue to behave like oppressors, because no one is more cruel than he with a guilty conscience, which he is trying to suppress or justify. The character of Israel is getting worse and worse as a result.<br>Think about 35 years of occupation - an entire generation raised without civil rights - that is totally injust and immoral. Thousands of Palestinians have been killed in the last few years by Israeli soldiers and settlers, including hundreds of children. Are you surprised that bombers try to punish Israelis after all this, including civilians?<br>The bombers are still wrong to kill civilians, and the US should step in. But it's difficult with the political situation here; our politicians are cowards. And most Americans and most American Jews, like the previous poster, don't know the facts and history! They try to claim the European press is anti-Semetic when they criticize Israel's worst abuses. They are in denial. Learn the history. Read Elias Chacour's book, "Blood Brothers."<br>Mr. Shashaa, great website. Keep up the good work.
		<div align="right">
		<i>6 August 2002</i>
		
			<i> - USA</i>
			
		</div>
		
		</font></td></tr>
		
		</tbody></table>
		
     <img src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/image/line1.gif">
   
			<table border="1" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="600">    
		<tbody><tr valign="top">
		
			<td width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b>reply to  -- -- &gt; </b>
			
					| <a href="mailto:cranebaker@hotmail.com" style="pointer-events: none;"><font color="#000000"><img border="0" src="/sites/palestinehistory.com/cgi-bin/comment/mail.gif"></font></a>
					
		</font></td></tr>
		
    <tr valign="top"> <td bgcolor="#fffff0" width="600">
			<font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000">
			
		What do you expect when you use a one ton bomb in the middle of a crowded city block. The Israeli army knew civilians would die and felt those lives were worth the end result. Is one terrorist worth 17 civilians? NO. Who are the terrorists anyhow? The Israeli state is equally to blame in the killing of innocent civilians. The Israeli people are filled with as much hate as the Palestinians and yet they are perceived as a democratic nation. What sort of democracy oppresses millions of Arabs giving them little in the way of humane treatment, civil rights and equal protection? Look at the record. Israel took its lands by force by terrorizing innocent Arabs. We should stop trying to pin labels on different groups of individuals. Terrorist, martyr, innocent civilians. What do they really mean anyhow? Who is really innocent in this struggle anyhow? The real answer is that both sides are not right or wrong, both sides have committed crimes and both sides deserve self-rule.<br>
		<div align="right">
		<i>25 July 2002</i>
		
			<i> - United States</i>
			
		</div>
		
		</font></td></tr>
		
		</tbody></table>
		
